---
import Adr from "../components/Adr.astro";
import Diagram from "../components/Diagram.astro";
import Excerpt from "../components/Excerpt.astro";
import Inferred from "../components/Inferred.astro";
import Layer from "../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import Path from "../components/Path.astro";
import Rule from "../components/Rule.astro";
import Sequence from "../components/Sequence.astro";
import Tree from "../components/Tree.astro";
import { firstPartyPlugins, manifestKinds } from "../lib/manifests.ts";

const P = "cli/src/iki_cli/plugin.py";
const D = "server/src/iki_server/plugins/deploy.py";
const kinds = manifestKinds();
const firstParty = firstPartyPlugins();

const boxes = [
  { id: "repo", x: 20, y: 40, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Plugin repository", sub: "YAML, scripts, tests" },
  { id: "validate", x: 200, y: 40, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Validate", sub: "schemas, then semantics" },
  { id: "migrations", x: 380, y: 40, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Migrations", sub: "iki plugin makemigrations" },
  { id: "tests", x: 560, y: 40, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Tests", sub: "actions, upgrade" },
  { id: "pin", x: 740, y: 40, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Pinned", sub: "plugins.lock.yaml" },
  { id: "wasm", x: 200, y: 170, w: 150, h: 60, label: "CEL via iki-wasm", sub: "rules type-checked" },
  { id: "preflight", x: 560, y: 170, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Preflight", sub: "against live records" },
  { id: "build", x: 740, y: 170, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Deployment build", sub: "apps + image", strong: true },
  { id: "migrate", x: 740, y: 300, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Migrate", sub: "one transaction", strong: true },
  { id: "sync", x: 560, y: 300, w: 150, h: 60, label: "sync_plugins", sub: "triggers, views, grants" },
  { id: "running", x: 380, y: 300, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Running", sub: "types, actions, UI" },
  { id: "detach", x: 200, y: 300, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Detach, purge", sub: "kept, frozen; tombstones" },
];
const edges = [
  { from: "repo", to: "validate" },
  { from: "validate", to: "migrations" },
  { from: "migrations", to: "tests" },
  { from: "tests", to: "pin" },
  { from: "validate", to: "wasm", label: "rules", dashed: true },
  { from: "pin", to: "build", label: "iki deploy build" },
  { from: "build", to: "preflight", dashed: true },
  { from: "build", to: "migrate", label: "migrate Job" },
  { from: "migrate", to: "sync" },
  { from: "sync", to: "running" },
  { from: "running", to: "detach", dashed: true },
];

const H = {
  short: "What a plugin is",
  how: "From a plugin repository to a running deployment",
  example: "The lots plugin, file by file",
  rules: "Kinds, builds, migrations, versions, Wasm and components",
  ref: "Commands and decisions",
};
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: H.short },
  { id: "how", label: H.how },
  { id: "deploy", label: "A deploy, step by step" },
  { id: "example", label: H.example },
  { id: "rules", label: H.rules },
  { id: "ref", label: H.ref },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title={H.short}>
    <p>
      A plugin is a git directory of YAML manifests and the scripts its actions run. It's checked
      against the iki/v1 spec, its migrations are written when it's authored and reviewed like code,
      and its actions are tested by running fixtures through the real worker. A deployment pins each
      plugin to a commit in its lockfile; <code>iki deploy build</code> compiles them all into
      Django apps inside the deployment's own image. On deploy, one database transaction applies
      every plugin's migrations together with the triggers and grants that guard their tables.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Plugins are deploy-time and trusted; there's no marketplace (<Adr n="0006" />).</li>
      <li>Declarations are data, behaviour is code: only actions run code, on workers (<Adr n="0032" />).</li>
      <li>Migrations keep history: nothing is ever dropped silently (<Adr n="0033" />).</li>
      <li>Each deployment pins plugins in a lockfile and builds its own image (<Adr n="0034" />).</li>
    </ul>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title={H.how}>
    <p>
      The top row happens in the plugin's own repository and CI; the rest happens in a deployment's
      config repository and cluster. The plugin template's CI runs the first steps (<Path
        p="plugin-template/.github/workflows/ci.yml"
      />); the config template's runs the build (<Path
        p="deploy/config-template/.github/workflows/build.yml"
      />).
    </p>
    <Diagram id="pluginlife" title="A plugin's life" width={910} height={380} boxes={boxes} edges={edges}>
      <div slot="repo">
        <p>
          <code>plugin.yaml</code> at the root, and each other kind of manifest in its own directory
          (<a href="/core-types/#kinds">the kinds</a>). Plugins are named <code
            >namespace/name</code
          >; <code>iki</code> is Iki's own (<Adr n="0113" />). A lab starts from the template (<Adr
            n="0039"
          />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="plugin-template" />, <Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/naming.py" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="validate">
        <p>
          Stage one checks each document against its JSON Schema and rewrites errors as plain
          sentences. Stage two checks what no schema can: references across files and the <code
            >--with</code
          > plugins, identities, states and guards, table-name lengths, settings, rules, actions,
          workflows, triggers, components (<Adr n="0032" />). YAML is read strictly as 1.2.
        </p>
        <p><Path p={P} sym="def run_validate(" />, <Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/validate.py" sym="def load_plugin(" />, <Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/yamlsource.py" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="migrations">
        <p>
          Built into a temporary directory and run through Django's makemigrations against the dummy
          backend, with Iki's history rules on top: a deleted field or type is refused, renames
          carry to history, unit changes convert stored values, new history tables are append-only
          (<Adr n="0033" />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p={P} sym="def run_makemigrations(" />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/plugins/makemigrations.py" />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/plugins/operations.py" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="tests">
        <p>
          <code>ActionTest</code> documents in <code>tests/</code> run through <code
            >iki-worker run --local</code
          > with the input the server would build, then the output is checked (<Adr n="0093" />).
          <code>--upgrade-from REF</code> migrates a scratch database from an earlier commit and back,
          comparing every revision's values (<Adr n={[94, 158]} />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="cli/src/iki_cli/testing.py" />, <Path p="cli/src/iki_cli/upgrade_test.py" />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/plugins/upgrade_test.py" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="pin">
        <p>
          Each entry names a git URL, a path and a full commit, a state (<code>active</code>,
          <code>detached</code>, <code>purged</code>) and settings. A <code>local</code> entry is for
          development only (<Adr n="0034" />). Iki's own plugins may come from a mirror, which can
          only serve trees Iki published (<Adr n="0114" />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/lockfile.py" sym="def load_lock(" />, <Path p="deploy/config-template/deployments/staging/plugins.lock.yaml" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="wasm">
        <p>
          Rules and guards are CEL. The validator type-checks them through the same iki-wasm module
          the server and browser evaluate them with, so a rule that validates means the same
          everywhere (<Adr n={[127, 128]} />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/rules.py" sym="def type_check(" />, <Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/wasm.py" sym="EXPORTS" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="preflight">
        <p>
          An Org Admin checks a built <code>manifest.json</code> against the live records in one
          read-only snapshot, without running its migrations: required-field backfills, invalid
          values, unique clashes, records in removed states, and a sample for CEL rules. The deploy
          repeats it and refuses blocking findings nobody acknowledged (<Adr n="0181" />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/plugins/preflight.py" sym="def preview_manifest(" />, <Path p="cli/src/iki_cli/preflight.py" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="build">
        <p>
          Reads the lockfile, fetches only the pinned commits (https or ssh, no hooks, submodules or
          LFS), validates all plugins together, checks settings and that migrations are complete,
          and writes each plugin's app plus <code>iki_installed_plugins</code>. A Dockerfile puts
          them on Iki's image, root-owned and read-only (<Adr n="0034" />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="cli/src/iki_cli/deploy.py" sym="def run_build(" />, <Path p="codegen/src/iki_codegen/build.py" sym="def build(" />, <Path p="deploy/plugins.Dockerfile" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="migrate">
        <p>
          The chart's migrate Job runs before new pods start. After refusal checks, Iki's own
          migrations run; then one transaction covers purges, dropping the guards on changed tables,
          reversing migrations the build lacks, every plugin's migrations, <code>sync_plugins</code>
          and the grants (<Adr n="0134" />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p={D} sym="def migrate_deployment(" />, <Path p="deploy/helm/iki/templates/migrate-job.yaml" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="sync">
        <p>
          Puts back what the database enforces for the installed plugins: HRID sequences, column
          comments, the <code>iki_views</code> views, unique and rule triggers, and the lock triggers
          on state-bearing types (<Adr n={[120, 127]} />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/plugins/sync.py" sym="def sync(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="running">
        <p>
          The server imports the generated apps and refuses a build made by another Iki version.
          Plugins' web components are served by digest into sandboxed frames (<Adr n={[34, 84]} />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/settings.py" sym="iki_installed_plugins" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="detach">
        <p>
          A detached plugin's tables lose INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE for the app role; its data is
          kept and readable (<Adr n="0091" />). Purging it needs a dry-run report, a reason, the
          typed name and a wait (30 days by default, at least 7), respects legal holds, and leaves
          tombstones; the next deploy drops its tables (<Adr n="0092" />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/plugins/purge.py" />, <Path p={D} sym="def _purge(" /></p>
      </div>
    </Diagram>

    <h3 id="deploy">A deploy, step by step</h3>
    <p>What happens between a merged lockfile change and new pods serving it.</p>
    <Sequence
      id="deploy-seq"
      title="A deploy of a plugin change"
      width={900}
      actors={[
        { id: "repo", label: "Config repo", sub: "CI" },
        { id: "build", label: "iki deploy build" },
        { id: "cluster", label: "Cluster", sub: "GitOps applies" },
        { id: "job", label: "Migrate Job" },
        { id: "db", label: "Postgres" },
      ]}
      steps={[
        { id: "pr", from: "repo", to: "build", label: "every PR: build and check the pinned plugins" },
        { id: "image", from: "repo", to: "repo", label: "on merge: verify Iki's signatures, build, sign, pin by digest" },
        { id: "apply", from: "repo", to: "cluster", label: "image.yaml updated; Argo CD or Flux applies the chart" },
        { id: "job", from: "cluster", to: "job", label: "the migrate Job runs before new pods" },
        { phase: "migrate_deployment" },
        { id: "refuse", from: "job", to: "job", label: "refuse: newer Iki, missing plugin, changed migration…" },
        { id: "own", from: "job", to: "db", label: "Iki's own migrations, each in its transaction" },
        { id: "one", from: "job", to: "db", label: "one transaction: purges, plugins' migrations, sync, grants" },
        { id: "pods", from: "cluster", to: "cluster", label: "new pods; a too-powerful role never turns ready" },
      ]}
    >
      <div slot="pr"><p>Fetches each plugin at its commit and fails on a plugin whose migrations don't match its manifests, a missing dependency, or an active plugin that depends on a detached one.</p><p><Path p="cli/src/iki_cli/deploy.py" sym="def _detached_alone(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="image"><p>The config template's workflow verifies Iki's images with cosign before building on them (<Adr n="0017" />).</p><p><Path p="deploy/config-template/.github/workflows/build.yml" />, <Path p="deploy/config-template/plugins.Dockerfile" /></p></div>
      <div slot="apply"><p>Configuration is GitOps per deployment; data moves between deployments only in bundles (<Adr n="0015" />).</p><p><Path p="deploy/config-template/README.md" /></p></div>
      <div slot="job"><p>The Job runs as the migrator role, the only one that owns tables (<Adr n="0025" />).</p><p><Path p="deploy/helm/iki/templates/migrate-job.yaml" /></p></div>
      <div slot="refuse"><p>Also refused: a non-atomic migration, and blocking preflight findings not acknowledged in the chart's <code>acknowledgePreflight</code> (<Adr n="0181" />).</p><p><Path p={D} sym="def _check_preflight(" />, <Path p="deploy/helm/iki/values.yaml" sym="acknowledgePreflight" /></p></div>
      <div slot="own"><p>Some of Iki's own migrations build indexes <code>CONCURRENTLY</code>, which can't run inside a transaction.</p></div>
      <div slot="one"><p>So a deploy's migrations and the guards that hold its records are applied or rolled back together: no moment where a table exists without its lock triggers (<Adr n="0134" />). A rollback never loses data: it changes nothing and says why if it would (<Adr n="0034" />).</p><p><Path p={D} sym="def _unguard(" />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/core/management/commands/grant_app_privileges.py" /></p></div>
      <div slot="pods"><p>Readiness checks the app role's privileges (<Adr n="0025" />).</p><p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/core/db_roles.py" /></p></div>
    </Sequence>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={3} title={H.example}>
    <p>
      <Path p="plugins/lots" label="iki/lots" /> is a mid-sized first-party plugin: nine types, six
      actions, triggers that recompute lots, one component, and five migrations. Its files, as git has
      them:
    </p>
    <Tree dir="plugins/lots" depth={2} />
    <p>Its manifest declares which Iki it works with and the types it needs, by schema version rather than commit (<Adr n={[16, 95]} />):</p>
    <Excerpt file="plugins/lots/plugin.yaml" start="^dependencies:" />
    <p>
      A setting a deployment chooses, here which review flow plasmid verifications use. It's read at
      build time from the deployment's settings file and checked against this declaration:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file="plugins/lots/plugin.yaml" start="^  verification_flow:" />
    <p>
      The component that shows a prep's verifications in a tab, and offers the plugin's own action
      on it (<Adr n="0170" />):
    </p>
    <Excerpt file="plugins/lots/components/prep_verifications.yaml" start="^kind:" />
    <p>
      In a deployment, it's one line of the lockfile. On the dev cluster it's a local directory, so
      editing it rebuilds the cluster's image; a real deployment pins a commit:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file="deploy/dev/plugins.lock.yaml" start="^  - \{ name: iki/lots" />
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={4} title={H.rules}>
    <div class="rules">
      <Rule title="What a plugin can declare" open>
        <p>The kinds, read from the validator:</p>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Lives in</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>{kinds.map((k) => <tr><td><code>{k.kind}</code></td><td><code>{k.directory}</code></td></tr>)}</tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          Two more documents have schemas but aren't plugin manifests: <code>ActionTest</code> in a
          plugin's <code>tests/</code>, and <code>PluginLock</code>, the lockfile. Lab roles are a
          <code>roles:</code> key in <code>plugin.yaml</code>, not a kind (<Adr n="0116" />). Units are
          UCUM, parsed by Iki's own code over the unmodified essence file (<Path
            p="spec/src/iki_spec/units/__init__.py"
          />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="What a build produces">
        <p>
          One package per plugin, <code>iki_plugin_&lt;namespace&gt;__&lt;name&gt;</code>: <code
            >apps.py</code
          >, <code>models.py</code>, <code>manifest.json</code>, <code>settings.json</code> for a
          deployment, the plugin's own migrations copied unchanged, and its components checked
          against their digests. Beside them, <code>iki_installed_plugins</code> lists the apps in
          dependency order with the Iki version that built them. The output is byte-for-byte
          deterministic (<Adr n="0033" />, <Path p="codegen/src/iki_codegen/build.py" />).
        </p>
        <p>
          The core plugin is built the same way by <code>make core</code> into <Path
            p="server/src/iki_plugin_iki__core"
          />, and a test fails while that app is behind its manifests (<Path
            p="scripts/build_core.py"
          />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Migrations keep history">
        <p>
          A field is never deleted: it's marked <code>removed: true</code>, or answered as a rename.
          A history column changes type only if its old values still fit. A unit change converts
          current and historical values and records it, so signatures read through it (<Adr
            n={[33, 148]}
          />). A state a plugin removes must say where its records go (<Adr n="0121" />). The
          operations are API: <Path p="server/src/iki_server/plugins/operations.py" sym="class ConvertUnit" />.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Versions and compatibility">
        <p>
          <code>iki:</code> in <code>plugin.yaml</code> says which Iki releases it works with, checked
          by validate, build and deploy, and again by the migrate Job. Dependencies constrain entity
          schema versions, not commits, because commits can't be ordered. The upgrade test fails if
          what a type's entities may hold changed and its <code>schema_version</code> didn't go up (<Adr
            n={[16, 95]}
          />).
        </p>
        <p>
          <Adr n="0016" /> names an <code>iki plugin upgrade</code> command that applies codemods. It
          doesn't exist in <Path p="cli/src/iki_cli" />.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Wasm: modules, not plugin code">
        <p>
          Plugins don't ship Wasm of their own. Their CEL is checked and evaluated by iki-wasm. A few
          first-party actions call standalone modules (primer checks, digests, annotation) under
          wasmtime; <code>iki deploy build</code> takes each from <code>iki_spec</code>, checks it
          against the digest the plugin keeps in git, and refuses a missing or mismatched one, so
          workers need no Rust (<Path p="cli/src/iki_cli/workers.py" />, <Path
            p="plugins/dna/data/oligo-checks.wasm.sha256"
          />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="First-party plugins and their trees">
        <p>
          First-party plugins live in this repository with their own versions, and must validate
          with their dependencies, have matching migrations, build, migrate forwards and back, and
          store entities (<Adr n="0039" />). <code>make first-party</code> appends each plugin's
          current git tree to <Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/first_party_trees.json" />, which only
          grows; a mirror may serve an <code>iki/*</code> plugin only at one of those trees (<Adr
            n="0114"
          />, <Path p="scripts/first_party_trees.py" sym="def tree(" />). There are {firstParty.length}
          today: <a href="/first-party-plugins/">the generated list</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          First-party images are built and signed like Iki's own, from <code
            >plugins/&lt;plugin&gt;/images/</code
          > (<Adr n="0065" />, <Path p="plugins/protein/images" />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Web components">
        <p>
          A component is one bundled ES module, at most 10 MiB, declaring its element, slots and
          events. The build copies it with its digest and the server checks it again before serving
          (<Adr n="0084" />). Components with source under <code>web/</code> are bundled by <Path
            p="scripts/bundle-plugin-components.mjs"
          />, and <code>pnpm test</code> fails on a stale bundle (<Adr n="0191" />). <Inferred
            why="They have no web/ source directory; nothing says how they were written."
            >The lots and template components are checked-in JavaScript, written by hand.</Inferred
          >
        </p>
      </Rule>
    </div>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title={H.ref}>
    <div class="refs">
      <div>
        <h3>Commands</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><code>iki plugin validate</code> <Path p={P} sym="def run_validate(" label="plugin.py" /></li>
          <li><code>iki plugin build</code> <Path p={P} sym="def run_build(" label="plugin.py" /></li>
          <li><code>iki plugin makemigrations</code> <Path p={P} sym="def run_makemigrations(" label="plugin.py" /></li>
          <li><code>iki plugin test</code> <Path p="cli/src/iki_cli/testing.py" label="testing.py" /></li>
          <li><code>iki plugin preflight</code> <Path p="cli/src/iki_cli/preflight.py" label="preflight.py" /></li>
          <li><code>iki deploy build</code> <Path p="cli/src/iki_cli/deploy.py" sym="def run_build(" label="deploy.py" /></li>
          <li><code>iki-server migrate_deployment</code> <Path p="server/src/iki_server/plugins/management/commands/migrate_deployment.py" label="command" /></li>
          <li><code>make core</code>, <code>make first-party</code> <Path p="Makefile" /></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Decisions</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><Adr n="0006" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0032" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0033" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0034" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0093" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0094" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0114" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0134" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0181" title /></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Skills for plugin authors</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><Path p="plugin-template/.claude/skills" /></li>
          <li><Path p="plugin-template/README.md" /></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
